The legal texts in this repository are official acts of the Kingdom of Belgium. Official acts of the authorities
are not protected by copyright in Belgium (Code de droit économique, art. XI.172, § 2).

They come from Justel, the consolidated legislation of the SPF Justice (Moniteur belge / Belgisch Staatsblad):

  Source: Justel, https://www.ejustice.just.fgov.be/cgi_loi/welcome.pl?language=fr, read through
  - legalize-be (Legalize, https://github.com/legalize-dev/legalize-be, commit
    da37dfb18b17b06f8f8dc74c0d724cca22292bee), whose data licence is "Licence ouverte / open data fédéral belge
    (CC0 par défaut)" and whose pipeline is under the MIT License (https://github.com/legalize-dev/legalize-pipeline);
    each of its files names its official Justel source in its YAML front matter;
  - Internet Archive captures of Justel pages (https://web.archive.org/), retrieved 28-29 October 2026.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per line;
Justel's inline notes and change markers were removed from the text and used to date and credit each change;
typesetting differences between Justel versions were normalised to Justel's latest rendering; words annulled by
the Constitutional Court were removed from the day the ruling was published; and the versions were arranged as git
commits credited to the acts that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither the SPF
Justice nor Legalize endorses this repository. It is not an official publication.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
